The forward lens copies an optional field (from.count, line 7 of 1.0) that the
data lacks, so its result would be incomplete. Before lens totality was proven
at bind, only Translate found it, and wrapped the evaluator's error with
fmt.Errorf so that its position (the mapping itself) survived only as text.

Bind now refuses the lens (checkLensTotality) at the mapping, as a structured
position, together with the bound the copy also narrows (count: int & <10,
line 3), which the data in this case happens not to exercise.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count?: int
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count: int & <10
}

forward: {
	count: from.count
}

backward: {
	count: to.count
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count: int & <10
}

forward: {
	count: from.count
}

backward: {
	count: to.count
}
-- data.json --
{"title": "a"}
-- out/error --
count in the result of lens 0.0->1.0 is not total for some instance:
    ship/history/1.0.thema:7:9
-- out/positions --
count in the result of lens 0.0->1.0 is not total for some instance
	authored ship/history/1.0.thema:7:9
